{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>which we have heard</b> — This is from many righteous people, and a person is obligated to accept what they transmitted, since the tradition was like established knowledge, and this is \"and we will know them.\"" "<b>And the meaning of \"those who recount\"</b> — Those who recount were our friends and they are our fathers, who have no desire to cause us to stumble."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:53.992557575Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}